unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1013038","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"193ab188feab878e79d7266489f490f07e5eb5923857b9f8a9eee2cb7666ae7d","compact":"34eb0c2deb201e55afc8719f37fd119298a7ce300bb076fe3548f959f12f934b","nasal":"34eb0c2deb201e55afc8719f37fd119298a7ce300bb076fe3548f959f12f934b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-13-39","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":13,"verse":39,"english":"Having completed that sacrifice, that perpetuator of his race, and foremost of men, the king, conferied on the priests the earth; and having conferred it, that auspicious descendant of Ikşvāku experienced high delight. And then the priests spoke to that monarch, who had all his sins purged off saying. You alone are worthy to protect the entire world. We do not want the earth; nor can we rule it, being, O lord of Earth, constantly engaged in Vedic studies. Do you, therefore, confer upon us something instead, as the price thereof.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.424,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-14-34","DUTT-1-14-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1013039","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2ecb1734317d52d5be667401ef1f774d4e1b8aaad754620352906d413d2f50fd","compact":"b3b5d10a885db2375c16a3a2416108b877d02fcd9095c1b7ee94ab33d49ea399","nasal":"1f895042bab92ccbf1f22132dc6b8e8ae96ccbf41091a12407802e10f7bc310b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-13-40","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":13,"verse":40,"english":"You alone are worthy to protect the entire world. We do not want the earth; nor can we rule it, being, O lord of Earth, constantly engaged in Vedic studies. Do you, therefore, confer upon us something instead, as the price thereof.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.835,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-14-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1013040","sanskritFile":"Ram01.t